{"kind": "mask", "attachment": [1, 1, 0], "findings": [{"level": "error", "title": "The model is too big", "body": "A mask should not exceed 10x10x5 voxels, but yours is 3x14x2.", "voxels": []}, {"level": "error", "title": "2 voxels are almost black", "body": "Trove's style guide asks for nothing darker than (10, 10, 10) - pure black reads as a hole in game. Use a dark grey instead.", "voxels": [4, 36]}, {"level": "error", "title": "The mask isn't far enough in front of its attachment point", "body": "The attachment point should be 6 voxels behind the mask (that space is the head); yours is 0.", "voxels": []}, {"level": "warning", "title": "3 voxels are not connected to the model", "body": "These only touch the rest of the model at a corner, or not at all. Trove renders them, but the style guide asks for face-connected geometry.", "voxels": [1, 2, 36]}, {"level": "warning", "title": "The mask is off-centre on the face", "body": "There shouldn't be more than ~5 voxels to any side of the attachment point; yours reaches 1 right, 1 left, 12 up, 1 down.", "voxels": []}], "satisfied": ["A blueprint stores one material per voxel, so alpha-on-solid and specular-on-glass - two of the classic .qb mistakes - can't happen here.", "Attachment point recorded at (1, 1, 0)."], "counts": {"error": 3, "warning": 2, "info": 0}}